# Polish a JEE sim (3 critics, one sim per tab)

Full procedure, critic principle blocks, verification bar and output contract:
**`.cursor/commands/polish-sims.md`** → which executes
**`.claude/skills/polish-sims/SKILL.md`**. Read both before editing. This rule
is the short form for when the command isn't invoked explicitly.

## The flow

Phase 0 gate baseline + `__audit` ratchet → Critic 1 physics (independent
oracle in `$TMPDIR`, re-run the sim's math) → Critic 2 pedagogy (spoiler sweep
incl. welcome blurb/voiceover; gated-card leak check) → Critic 3 visuals (REAL
screenshots via `tools/cdp.mjs`, both themes; `ctx.font` must never contain a
literal `var(--…)`) → consolidate with ORCHESTRATOR RULINGS in
`$TMPDIR/<base>.polish/findings.md` → apply fixes surgically → re-run the
ENTIRE bar → ledger row.

## Hard rules

- ONE file only; scratch in `$TMPDIR`; no git; never push to S3.
- The four user-version layers (welcome overlay, guided inquiry, controls
  guide, voiceover) must survive — the jsdom ×3 + `user-version-eval.mjs`
  battery proves it.
- `window.__audit` pass-set identical before/after (the ratchet).
- Never `disabled` on sim parameter controls (shell `gateLocksPlay` transport
  disable is sanctioned; `__freeExplore` must re-enable ▶).
- No third-party sim-source names.
- Known-benign, do not flag: jsdom KaTeX CSS parse noise, favicon 404,
  per-step staged reveals, gateLocksPlay, draw-after-Play idle blankness.

## Verify (all PASS before reporting)

`node --check` every script · 3 jsdom verifiers with
`--baseline <(git show 6ba6f47:"<path>")` · `node tools/user-version-eval.mjs
<port> "<module-path>"` · live `__audit` == ratchet · copyright grep clean ·
per-fix live probes re-run. Unique CDP port per tab (12700 + concept mod 200).
Pixel probes target `#sceneCanvas`, never the first `<canvas>` (hidden hero).

Report: verdict → per-critic counts → best catch → gate scorecard →
`REVIEW-LOG.md` row → end with `S3: re-push required for this file`.
